></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="6" rect="595.276001,160.459732,779.276001,252.459732"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251013091345+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="122730b3-1b25-4775-a3f9-e247604a3f39" date="D:20251013091345+10'00'" name="ff678a08-396b-4102-9056-31b3cb8295b9" icon="Comment" page="6" rect="310.087341,228.765366,334.087341,252.765366" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Thus, support or developmental&#xD;initiatives, for high-performance sport coaches&#xD;should remain cognizant that a broad behavioral repertoire&#xD;(e.g. a mix of light and dark) is possibly useful&#xD;for the effectiveness of coaching leaders in their specific&#xD;context.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>4,7,30 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This is in contradiction with advocacy for&#xD;over-emphasis on bright-type leadership approaches&#xD;suggested elsewhere (e.g., transformational leadership),&#xD;although consistent with comments made in the introduction&#xD;of this paper.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>31&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This work has shown that the assessment of coaches&#xD;in high-performance sport environment using regular,&#xD;and valid, workplace measures and concepts at a normative&#xD;level has a degree of utility not otherwise clearly&#xD;evidenced in the field.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="6" rect="595.276001,160.765381,779.276001,252.765381"
/></text
></annots
><f href="../pdfs/10.1177_1747954120964059.pdf"
/><ids original="D7E8E423E4341F2A1312365F060390C2" modified="263DCDF278AB875F174AE2DBE0839B1E"
/></xfdf
>